- Tool 1: DirBuster
    - 
    - https://www.kali.org/tools/dirbuster/
    - Seeks out hidden directories or files on web servers. Can brute force some things with dictionary attacks.
    - Categorie(s)
        - Web Application Testing
        - Reconnaissance
        - Pen Testing
    - It is a java based tool, so can work anything that runs a Java Runtime (JRE)
        - Linux
        - Windows
        - Mac
    - Use Case(s)
        - Authorized security assessments, 
    - Strengths / Limits:
        - Strenghts:
            - Multi-threaded
            - Ships with large built-in wordlists
            - Supports recursive scanning, file extension fuzzing, and pure brute force mode
            - Free and open source
            - Beginner Friendly
        - Limits
            - Effectively unmaintained; the last release dates back many years
            - Java GUI is heavier than CLI alternatives
            - Weaker handling of modern setups
            - Faster, more flexible alternatives exist

